  "mathematical_review": {
    "signed_overlap": "rho is still arbitrary signed; effectiveCoefficient remains the same two original Rosser evaluations. The explicit abs_of_nonneg witness is only 0 <= (t.1.1 : Real), the natural denominator, and neither assumes nor rewrites a signed coefficient as nonnegative. Zero natural denominators remain covered by totalized division; no selector/positivity assumption is added to the unconditional absolute bound.",
    "carrier_and_truncation": "The full divisors of P, residual P/p1, both rho(e)/rho(p1*e) branches and original strict tests on e versus p1*e remain unchanged. Both physical caps multiplier*e and multiplier*(p1*e) are retained. No multiplicativity/Euler-product or artificial unit-bound premise is introduced.",
    "multiplicity": "The complete labelled tuple carrier S and product fibres, repeated primes, arbitrary marked subfamilies and rank^rank fibre bound remain exact. Product weight is still the signed weighted sum over a fibre, not an unweighted image.",
    "beta_fix": "change N-m=N-r at heq merely exposes the original complement-map equality; existing strict m<N,r<N bounds and omega are retained. No new domain constraint or counting assumption appears.",
    "weights_quantifiers_and_cutoffs": "Existing hB>=0 and upper bound W<=B are unchanged; no W>=0 hypothesis is added to the weighted finite Fubini/small-prime theorem. The original inclusive product cap, strict m<N and N-m<z guards, B*rank^rank*z bound, signed test functions and quantifier order are unchanged.",
    "new_analytic_claims": "None: no source-mass, U-star, distribution or asymptotic estimate is supplied by these API/beta repairs."
  },
